title: Downcycling
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Most of what gets called recycling is this.

A material goes around again, and comes out worse. Paper fibers get shorter every time they are pulped. Mixed plastics get melted together into a lower grade of plastic that can only become a park bench or a speed bump. After that there is no next step.

[[Cradle to Cradle]] names it. Downcycling slows the trip to the landfill. It doesn't cancel it.

A [[Tetra Pak]] carton shredded and pressed into roof board is downcycled. So is the [[PolyAl]] left over from one.

The opposite is a [[Technical Nutrient]] that keeps its quality each time around, like [[Aluminum]] on its own.

See [[Recycle]], [[The Upcycle]], [[Recycling comes last]]
